// prism_ui_token -- tags/chips (prism/ui/ composition layer): tag, closable tag, tag group, tag
// input. Every one is a COMPOSITION over the closed 22-primitive vocabulary (widget/), built
// through prism_ui_kit.nova's helpers wherever they fit -- no new PrismNodeKind (PRISM_SPEC.md
// axiom A7), same discipline as prism_ui_feedback.nova / prism_ui_input.nova before it.
//
// ── WHY TAGS GET THEIR OWN FILE: THIS IS THE MOST COMMON CATEGORICAL WIDGET IN ADMIN UIs ───────
// A status pill ("Active"/"Pending"/"Failed"), a category label, a search filter chip, a
// multi-value form field's current selection -- every admin dashboard in the "Ant-Design-class
// component" set this campaign is targeting (ui/README.md) reaches for a tag dozens of times per
// screen, far more often than any single feedback or overlay component does. It earns a dedicated
// file for the same reason prism_ui_feedback.nova and prism_ui_data.nova did: high reuse density,
// small closed surface, worth getting exactly right once rather than re-derived ad hoc at every
// call site (this is precisely the LOC-and-correctness argument prism_ui_kit.nova's own header
// makes for `prism_ui_collect` -- a widely reused shape is a liability until it is factored once).
//
// ── WHY VARIANT IS A CLOSED 4-VALUE ENUM, NOT A STRING ──────────────────────────────────────────
// Same reasoning as PrismNodeKind / PrismMeshTrack / PrismIcon / prism_ui_feedback's own
// PrismFbSeverity: a free-form variant string ("succes", a typo, silently renders as an unstyled
// default) is a RUNTIME surprise; the enum makes an invalid variant a COMPILE error instead.
// Variants are `Tk`-prefixed (`TkDefault`, not `Default`) to match the exact convention
// `PrismFbSeverity` established for this same reason (`FbInfo`, not `Info` -- prism_content.nova's
// `PrismIcon` already owns a bare `Info()`/`Warning()` pair). Recorded honestly rather than
// overclaimed: MB.2x's own probe (`prism_ui_feedback.nova`'s history) directly tested whether two
// enums declaring the SAME bare variant name actually collide in NOVA's flat LLVM symbol space,
// and found they do NOT -- variant constructors are mangled per-enum, so the original collision
// fear was disproven. The `Tk` prefix is kept anyway, for the reason that survives that finding:
// consistency with every other closed-enum module in this tree (`PrismFbSeverity`, `PrismEntryKind`,
// `PrismColumnPin`, ...) all follow the identical prefixed-variant convention, and a reader scanning
// this file next to those should not have to wonder why THIS one enum is the exception.
//
// ── WHY close_label IS MANDATORY, NEVER A DEFAULT "Remove"/"×" ─────────────────────────────────
// PRISM_SPEC.md §13's a11y requirement (already the reason prism_interact.nova's
// press/flag/range/link all require an explicit accessible-name parameter, and the reason
// prism_ui_feedback.nova's confirm dialog rejects both of its button labels rather than defaulting
// to "OK"/"Cancel"): a close button with no caller-supplied name is a button a screen reader
// announces as nothing more than "button" -- indistinguishable from every OTHER close button on
// the page. `close_label` exists so a caller writes "Remove tag: Urgent", not "×", and this
// constructor rejects an empty one for the identical reason `prism_press` itself already rejects a
// control with neither a label nor children: an unlabelled interactive control is unusable, not
// merely unstyled.
//
// ── WHY tag_input REJECTS DUPLICATE TAG STRINGS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Identical reasoning to `prism_structure.prism_each` rejecting a duplicate row key and
// `prism_interact.prism_pick` rejecting a duplicate option value (both already established in this
// tree): a tag list is presented to the user as a SET of distinct values, and two entries reading
// "urgent" would make "remove the 'urgent' tag" an ambiguous instruction -- which physical chip
// does the close button on the DUPLICATE remove? Rather than let that ambiguity reach a renderer
// (or a future reactivity layer keying off tag identity), it is rejected at construction with a
// typed error naming the exact duplicate, using the same "seen dict, reject the second occurrence"
// idiom `prism_pick` and `prism_in_multiselect` already use for their own duplicate checks.
//
// ── WHY THE GROUP IS A `flow`, NOT A `band` ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// PRISM_SPEC.md §7 gives `band` and `flow` both an inline axis; the difference `prism_arrange.nova`
// itself documents is that `flow` is the one that WRAPS. A row of tags is exactly the case that
// motivates that distinction: a filter bar with a dozen category chips must not force a horizontal
// scrollbar (or silently overflow its container) the moment the viewport narrows -- and Prism has
// no media queries to rescue a `band` there (§11 deliberately has no cascade, per
// prism_ui_kit.nova's own `prism_ui_labeled` header note making the identical point about
// label-beside-control layouts). `flow` is the layout that degrades gracefully at every width;
// `band` is not, so `prism_tk_tag_group` is built on `prism_arrange.prism_flow`, never `prism_band`.
//
// ── WHY THIS FILE IMPORTS `prism_node` DIRECTLY, UNLIKE ANY EARLIER `ui/` MODULE ─────────────────
// Every `ui/` component built so far composes exclusively through `widget/`'s own smart
// constructors (`prism_arrange`, `prism_content`, `prism_interact`, `prism_structure`) and never
// touches `prism_node` itself -- verified by grep across the whole `ui/` tree before writing this
// file (CLAUDE.md's "does this already exist" discipline, applied to a PATTERN rather than a
// function). That holds because no earlier `ui/` component needed to attach a component-specific
// attr onto an arrangement primitive that `widget/` itself deliberately keeps attr-free.
// `prism_arrange.prism_band(children)` is that kind of deliberate thin wrapper: its own header
// states plainly that `stack`/`band`/`layer`/`flow` carry NO attrs anywhere in PRISM_SPEC.md Part
// III, so its signature is `children: list` with no attrs parameter at all -- correctly, for what
// `widget/` alone needs to represent. A tag's `variant`, though, is real information a THEMING
// layer needs to read back off the node (which visual treatment to paint), and there is nowhere in
// `widget/`'s surface to attach it short of going one layer down to the constructor `prism_arrange`
// itself is built on: `prism_node.prism_node_branch(kind, attrs, children)`. That function is
// PUBLIC API on `prism_node.nova` for exactly this shape (its own header lists it as one of four
// constructors, not an internal), and `prism_structure.nova` already reaches for it directly at the
// `widget/` layer itself (`prism_sheet`'s `{"exclusive": exclusive}`, `prism_grid`'s per-row
// `{}`-attrs `Band`) whenever a primitive it composes needs an attr `prism_arrange`/`prism_content`/
// `prism_interact` don't expose. Using it here is the identical move, one layer up: still a `Band`
// (PrismNodeKind is untouched, axiom A7 holds), just decorated with metadata `prism_arrange`'s own
// thin wrapper has no parameter to carry.
//
// PUBLIC API
//   Variant (closed, 4 values -- see header)
//     PrismTagVariant                                    TkDefault()|TkPrimary()|TkSuccess()|TkDanger()
//     prism_tk_variant_default() / _primary() / _success() / _danger()   cross-module ctors
//     prism_tk_variant_name(v) -> string   exhaustive: "default"|"primary"|"success"|"danger"
//   Components (all Result<PrismNode>; every one validates, none fails silently)
//     prism_tk_tag(label, variant) -> band(variant attr) containing [label]
//       rejects an empty label
//     prism_tk_tag_closable(label, variant, close_label) -> band(variant attr) containing
//       [label, close-press(icon=Close)]
//       rejects an empty label or an empty close_label (a11y, see header)
//     prism_tk_tag_group(tags: list) -> flow(tags)
//       tags: list<PrismNode> (bare list, runtime-checked). rejects an empty list and a
//       non-PrismNode element
//     prism_tk_tag_input(label, tags: list, max_tags: int?) -> stack containing
//       [tag_flow (omitted if tags is empty), entry field (omitted once at capacity)]
//       tags: list<string> (bare list, runtime-checked); each existing tag renders as a closable
//       chip whose close_label names the specific tag ("Remove tag: <value>"). rejects an empty
//       label, a non-string tag element, a duplicate tag string, and a negative max_tags
//   Accessor
//     prism_tk_tag_variant_of(node) -> string   the stored "variant" attr (attr_str, default
//       "default" if absent -- mirrors prism_node.nova's own typed-getter convention)

import prism_node
import prism_arrange
import prism_content
import prism_interact
import prism_ui_kit

// ── Variant: closed, 4 values (see header) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
enum PrismTagVariant
    TkDefault()
    TkPrimary()
    TkSuccess()
    TkDanger()

fn prism_tk_variant_default() -> PrismTagVariant
    TkDefault()
fn prism_tk_variant_primary() -> PrismTagVariant
    TkPrimary()
fn prism_tk_variant_success() -> PrismTagVariant
    TkSuccess()
fn prism_tk_variant_danger() -> PrismTagVariant
    TkDanger()

// Exhaustive, no wildcard arm -- adding a 5th variant without a case here is a compile error, same
// payoff PrismFbSeverity's own exhaustive name match gets from the identical shape.
fn prism_tk_variant_name(v: PrismTagVariant) -> string
    match v
        TkDefault() => "default"
        TkPrimary() => "primary"
        TkSuccess() => "success"
        TkDanger() => "danger"

// ── Shared band-with-variant-attr builder (see header: why prism_node is imported directly) ────
// Factored to one place so `prism_tk_tag` and `prism_tk_tag_closable` cannot drift on the attr's
// exact key or on how the enum's name is derived.
fn _prism_tk_tag_band(variant: PrismTagVariant, children: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    let attrs = {"variant": prism_tk_variant_name(variant)}
    prism_node.prism_node_branch(prism_node.prism_kind_band(), attrs, children)

// ── Tag: non-interactive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fn prism_tk_tag(label: string, variant: PrismTagVariant) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(label) == 0
        return err("prism_tk_tag: label must not be empty")
    let lbl = prism_content.prism_label(label)?
    _prism_tk_tag_band(variant, [lbl])

// ── Tag: closable ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See header for why close_label is mandatory. The close button's visual content is the Close
// glyph from the closed 12-icon set (prism_content.nova); its ACCESSIBLE name is close_label, not
// the glyph -- exactly the text/children split prism_press's own signature already makes.
fn prism_tk_tag_closable(label: string, variant: PrismTagVariant, close_label: string) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(label) == 0
        return err("prism_tk_tag_closable: label must not be empty")
    if len(close_label) == 0
        return err("prism_tk_tag_closable: close_label must not be empty -- a close button with no accessible name is invisible to a screen reader (PRISM_SPEC.md §13)")
    let lbl = prism_content.prism_label(label)?
    let close_icon = prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_content.prism_icon_close())?
    let close_btn = prism_interact.prism_press(close_label, [close_icon])?
    _prism_tk_tag_band(variant, [lbl, close_btn])

// ── Tag group ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See header for why `flow`, not `band`. `tags` is a bare `list` (not `list<PrismNode>`, mirroring
// prism_node.nova's own self-referential-generic caution -- see that file's header), so every
// element is guarded with the same `type_name(...) != "PrismNode"` check prism_node_new itself
// uses before its first field read, naming the offending index and actual type on rejection.
fn prism_tk_tag_group(tags: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(tags) == 0
        return err("prism_tk_tag_group: tags must not be empty")
    for idx, t in tags
        if type_name(t) != "PrismNode"
            return err("prism_tk_tag_group: tag " + str(idx) + " is not a PrismNode (got " + type_name(t) + ")")
    prism_arrange.prism_flow(tags)

// ── Tag input ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Validates `max_tags` (if present, must be >= 0) and reports whether the entry field must be
// hidden because `tags` has already reached the cap. Factored out of the main constructor so the
// "is this at capacity" question has exactly one answer, computed once, rather than re-derived at
// each of the two places that would otherwise need to ask it.
fn _prism_tk_input_at_capacity(tag_count: int, max_tags: int?) -> Result<bool>
    match max_tags
        None => ok(false)
        Some(n) =>
            if n < 0
                return err("prism_tk_tag_input: max_tags must be >= 0, got " + str(n))
            ok(tag_count >= n)

// Each existing tag renders as a closable chip (default variant) whose close button's accessible
// name identifies the SPECIFIC tag being removed -- e.g. "Remove tag: Urgent" -- exactly the
// example `prism_tk_tag_closable`'s own header gives for close_label, reused here rather than
// re-derived.
fn _prism_tk_input_chip(value: string) -> Result<PrismNode>
    prism_tk_tag_closable(value, prism_tk_variant_default(), "Remove tag: " + value)

// `tags`: bare `list` of strings (not `list<string>` -- same caution `prism_structure.prism_grid`
// applies to its own `columns: list<string>`-documented-but-bare-`list` parameter: a hostile or
// mistaken non-string element must be caught before it reaches `t in seen` / the chip builder,
// not assumed away by the doc comment). Checked in the order a caller would want to read them:
// type first (a wrong element kind makes every later check meaningless), then emptiness, then
// duplication -- so the FIRST bad tag in source order is always what gets named, never a later
// one found by accident of dict-iteration order.
fn prism_tk_tag_input(label: string, tags: list, max_tags: int?) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(label) == 0
        return err("prism_tk_tag_input: label must not be empty")
    let seen = {}
    for idx, t in tags
        if not is_string(t)
            return err("prism_tk_tag_input: tag " + str(idx) + " is not a string (got " + type_name(t) + ")")
        if len(t) == 0
            return err("prism_tk_tag_input: tag " + str(idx) + " must not be empty")
        if t in seen
            return err("prism_tk_tag_input: duplicate tag '" + t + "'")
        seen[t] = true
    let at_capacity = _prism_tk_input_at_capacity(len(tags), max_tags)?
    let parts = []
    if len(tags) > 0
        // A private top-level fn is wrapped in a lambda before being handed to
        // prism_ui_collect -- mirroring prism_ui_kit.nova's own `_prism_ui_kv_row` call site,
        // which does the identical wrap even though the helper's signature already matches
        // exactly; passing a bare top-level function name where a closure value is expected is
        // not a pattern used anywhere else in this tree, so this file does not introduce it.
        let mk = fn(tag_value) _prism_tk_input_chip(tag_value)
        let chips = prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_collect(tags, mk)?
        let flow = prism_arrange.prism_flow(chips)?
        parts.push(flow)
    if not at_capacity
        let entry = prism_interact.prism_entry(label, prism_interact.prism_entry_kind_text(), "")?
        parts.push(entry)
    prism_arrange.prism_stack(parts)

// ── Accessor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fn prism_tk_tag_variant_of(node: PrismNode) -> string
    prism_node.prism_node_attr_str(node, "variant", "default")
